Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20210915055358.19997-2-kishon@ti.com

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect definition of the `max-virtual-functions` property in the device tree for PCIe endpoint nodes, where it was mistakenly set as a 16-bit value instead of the required 8-bit value. This misconfiguration could lead to improper handling of virtual functions by the PCIe devices, potentially causing functionality issues or failures in recognizing the correct number of virtual functions.

